  <server name="firefox">
    Use tools from this server through `execute` under `tools["firefox"]`.
    Browse and debug the web with Firefox. Use this for any browser or web page task: opening a URL, automating a web flow, or debugging a page (console errors, network requests, DOM state). The task does not need to name Firefox, reach for these tools unless another browser is explicitly requested. Chrome-only browser tools do not control Firefox, do not assume they cover this.

    Enabled capabilities:
    - pages: Open, navigate, select, and close pages.
    - snapshot: Capture accessibility/DOM snapshots and resolve UIDs.
    - input: Interact with the page via UID-based clicks, typing, key presses, drag, and uploads.
    - screenshot: Capture screenshots of the page or specific elements.
    - print: Print the page to PDF.
    - downloads: Monitor and manage file downloads.
    - utilities: Handle dialogs, history navigation, and viewport sizing.
    - management: Inspect Firefox options and logs, and close the browser.
    - webextension: Install and uninstall web extensions.
    - screencast: Record screencasts of the page viewport (Firefox 154+).
    - script: Evaluate arbitrary JavaScript in the page context.

    When these tools are deferred, load the core set in one search rather than one at a time: list_pages, new_page, navigate_page, take_snapshot, get_page_text. Add task-specific tools to the same search: click_by_uid / fill_by_uid / hover_by_uid for interaction, screenshot_page / screenshot_by_uid for visuals, evaluate_script for one-off JS.
